

## Continuation update (2026-09-25; NameServer availability cleanup follow-up)

- Compared Java `getAvailableNameSrvList` and `scanAvailableNameSrv` with the Rust public getter and scan completion. Java returns the map snapshot without filtering configured addresses; it prunes removed keys at scan start and asynchronous per-address jobs may subsequently race to update availability.
- Rust now exposes the stored availability set as-is, preserves removed-address entries across list replacement, prunes at the next scan, and accepts outcomes of in-flight probes without a configured-list check (but still rejects outcomes after client shutdown). Added `p3_nameserver_update_prunes_availability_on_next_scan` for the observable cleanup boundary.
- Focused test passed; complete gates passed: `cargo test --workspace --locked --offline` (79 unit/integration tests plus doc tests), `cargo fmt --all --check`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked --offline -- -D warnings`, `python3 scripts/check-workspace-metadata.py`, `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test`, and `git diff --check`.
- Implementation commit `196e3bf` and compatibility/log commit `c1b085c`. Updated the inventory and ADR; scan executor topology, stale completion races, wrapper selection, callback/error, processor/hook, oneway and TLS global-configuration differences remain. No live Broker, Docker or Maven validation. Phase 3 acceptance is not met and Phase 4 remains blocked; P3-V04 remains for Phase 19.
